From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 13a] ppp: preserve original control provenance through IPv6 fragments

PRIVATE SOURCE PIECE. Apply after the exact Ze v7.3 series and frozen
0012 + 0012a. No constructor dispatch or capability bit 9 is activated.
Socket eligibility/copy and TX/multicast enforcement are separate pieces;
none of them may activate until the complete set is reviewed and proven.

Stamp the existing original PPP IPv6 receive producer after its final scrub.
Keep direct TCP and non-DHCP UDP untagged. Native ICMPv6 and extension/fragment
candidates retain provenance before native validation, never a second parser.
Fragment keys keep the nullable exact owner and RX/TX role even when native
GLOBAL-address keys clear iif. Existing Ze XFRM key and memory custody remain.

--- a/include/net/ppp_control.h
+++ b/include/net/ppp_control.h
@@ -48,4 +48,12 @@
 bool ppp_control_owner_live(const struct ppp_control_owner *owner,
 			    const struct net_device *dev);
+/* Caller owns a reference. current protects the original dev namespace read
+ * with its own RCU section; dev is borrowed and its internals need RCU/RTNL.
+ * Neither helper resolves a numeric label or acquires a netdevice reference.
+ */
+bool ppp_control_owner_current(const struct ppp_control_owner *owner);
+struct net_device *
+ppp_control_owner_dev(const struct ppp_control_owner *owner);
+unsigned int ppp_control_owner_size(const struct ppp_control_owner *owner);
 /* RTNL + live original owner required; returns an owned short net lease,
  * or NULL. The owner itself MUST NOT pin its unit's namespace lifetime.
@@ -65,2 +74,5 @@
